 "fieldData": {
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Work Order Form Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is a work order form?\", \"a\": \"A work order form is the document that turns a request for a repair or service into an assigned job. It says where the problem is and who will fix it by when. After the job, it holds the hours and parts used along with a sign-off. Maintenance and field service crews keep work order forms as the record of each job.\"}, {\"q\": \"How to make a work order form?\", \"a\": \"Start with the fields a technician relies on: the location, the problem, a photo, the priority, and the assignee. Add close-out fields for hours, parts, and a signature. Then describe those fields and your routing rules to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-form-builder'>AI form builder</a>, which builds the form along with a table of open jobs.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should a work order request form include?\", \"a\": \"A work order request form needs the exact location, a plain description of the problem, and a photo where one helps. Add a category and a phone number for follow-up questions. Leave the cost estimate and the assignee off the request; the supervisor who approves the job fills those in.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between a work request form and a work order form?\", \"a\": \"A work request form is how anyone reports a problem, whether a tenant or a front desk clerk. The request becomes a work order once a supervisor approves it and assigns a technician and a due date. Duplicates and out-of-scope requests get declined at that step. An app built with Emergent has no per-seat pricing, and every approver is included.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is a maintenance work order form?\", \"a\": \"A maintenance work order form records one repair or scheduled service task on a building or a piece of equipment. It names the asset and the technician, with a due date. Once the job closes, the same record holds the labor time and materials used. It applies as much to a rooftop HVAC unit as to a dripping faucet.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an example of a work order form?\", \"a\": \"A typical one starts with a leaking kitchen faucet in Unit 2A. The tenant files the request with a photo of the drip, and the order assigns a plumber for Tuesday morning. At close-out the plumber logs 45 minutes of labor and a $14 cartridge. The tenant then signs to confirm the leak has stopped.\"}, {\"q\": \"What should the close-out section of a work order form include?\", \"a\": \"The close-out section should include the labor hours, each part with its cost, and a line describing the repair. Add the completion date and a signature from the requester or a supervisor. Make each one required, since a half-recorded job is hard to bill. If closed jobs get billed, <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder/invoice-automation'>invoice automation</a> can turn each record into an invoice.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you track work order forms?\", \"a\": \"Give each work order a status, such as open, assigned, on hold, done, or canceled, and keep every order in one table you can filter. A canceled order stays in the table with its reason instead of being deleted. Filtering by unit or asset then shows the full repair history, including the jobs that never went ahead.\"}, {\"q\": \"Are digital work order forms better than paper ones?\", \"a\": \"For most crews, yes. A digital form reaches the assigned technician as soon as it is filed, with photos attached and each status change timestamped. Paper forms wait in a tray and get retyped before anyone can sort or bill them. Forms built with Emergent have no response cap, even in a month with several hundred requests.\"}, {\"q\": \"What types of work order forms are there?\", \"a\": \"The main types are maintenance, field service, construction, and IT or facilities requests. Maintenance forms cover repairs on buildings and equipment. Field service forms add the customer's signature and billable parts. Construction work orders set a scope and a spending limit for each subcontractor. Parts bought for any of them go on a separate purchase order form.\"}]}; </script></div></div>"
 }
